__INLINE:capture-contract.ts__
// Where a posted envelope is judged, and the only node on this canvas
// that judges an envelope at all. The library above is spliced in whole
// and holds the whole boundary: captureEnvelopeErrors is handed the
// posted body and answers one sentence per rule it broke, empty when
// the envelope is one the contract accepts. Nothing below states a rule
// of its own. What the five members are, what a provenance note may
// hold, and which spelling of a moment is accepted are settled in
// src/lib/capture-contract.ts and under test beside it.
//
// What the group below judges is a different question asked of a body
// this node has already accepted: whether the READING a parser_config
// makes of it is the one the source's own contract describes. An
// envelope is the wrapper and is this service's shape; a contract is
// the source's, and one row can fail either check with the other clean.
//
// THE ROW ALREADY EXISTS. Store Raw Capture wrote the request into
// documents.raw before this node ran, and nothing here re-runs that
// write. So a refusal is a stored failure rather than a lost capture:
// every sentence collected here lands in documents.parse_error on a row
// an operator can read, replay against a corrected config, and promote.
// That ordering is the whole reason this boundary is the third node on
// the canvas and not the first.
//
// A REFUSAL NAMES THE MEMBER AND THE RULE AND NEVER THE VALUE. Every
// sentence collected here is a whole constant out of
// capture-contract.ts. That module writes the five member names into
// itself and builds no sentence from a template, so there is no hole a
// posted value can arrive through, and this node joins what it was
// answered and composes nothing of its own.
//
// The rule is load bearing here in a way it is nowhere else on these
// canvases. This text is derived from a body no boundary has judged,
// and it is written into a column an operator reads: a template with a
// hole in it would render a stranger's bytes into a console, a review
// queue, or a digest, which is the one place nobody can go afterwards
// and take them out again. The same rule is why Store Raw Capture's own
// sentence is a constant, and why the version comparison below reports
// this service's number rather than the one that was posted.
//
// What a reader loses by that is WHICH member broke a family rule: a
// provenance note with three unusable names produces one sentence,
// because the second and third would be the identical constant. The
// trade holds because the whole envelope is sitting in documents.raw
// beside the sentence, which is where a value belongs, so a rule plus a
// member family is enough to go and find it.
// src/lib/capture-contract.ts argues the same trade from the other side
// and says what a parser config does instead, its field map being far
// larger with no stored copy of it beside the error.
//
// AN UNKNOWN CONTRACT VERSION IS REFUSED BY NAME. The library answers a
// version fault ALONE and judges nothing else, because the rules the
// other four members would be judged by are not the rules the client
// wrote to, so faults derived from them would name members the client
// did not get wrong. That makes the fault list past a version refusal a
// short list rather than a clean bill, and something on the item has to
// say so.
//
// contract_version_accepted is that member. False says the payload did
// not state, by own key, the exact version this service accepts, and it
// covers a payload with no keys, one stating no version, and one
// stating another number. In all three the four members below the
// version went unjudged, and their absence from the fault list is not a
// claim they are right. contract_version beside it is
// CAPTURE_CONTRACT_VERSION, this service's own constant, so a reader
// learns which version to write to without this node having repeated
// back what was posted.
//
// THE VERSION MEMBER IS READ ONLY TO SAY WHICH REFUSAL FIRED.
// statedVersion below reads one own key and compares it against an
// exported constant. It decides nothing: captureEnvelopeErrors is the
// whole judgment and its answer is what reaches the column. A rule
// restated here would be a second copy with nothing comparing it
// against the first, which is the same reason the sentences are joined
// rather than rewritten.
//
// PROVENANCE, AND WHERE IT GOES. An accepted envelope's four non-body
// members are the note: how the capture was taken, as the client
// described it, verbatim. They are read off CAPTURE_ENVELOPE_MEMBERS
// rather than written out, so a member added to the envelope joins the
// note by joining that tuple and this node needs no edit.
// src/sources/push-capture.ts derives its own note the same way and
// stores the same two member shape in documents.raw, which is what
// keeps a document captured through that adapter and one captured
// through this canvas the same row to read.
//
// record is the body as posted. The adapter splits a list body into one
// document per entry and stores one entry per row; a capture is one row
// here, so the member holds the body whole, and nothing is lost either
// way because the note and the record together are the envelope
// rearranged.
//
// The note is built for an ACCEPTED envelope and for no other. A
// refused one leaves documents.raw exactly as it was posted, which is
// the honest place for members nothing has judged: rearranging them
// into a note would file unexamined values under names that claim they
// were read.
//
// THE PROVISIONAL KEY DOES NOT MOVE WITH raw. documents.hash was
// written by Store Raw Capture over the body as posted, and it is a
// column rather than a derivation, so the node below rewriting raw
// leaves the key where it is. A second POST of the same capture
// computes the same provisional key, conflicts with the same row, and
// resolves to it.
//
// NOTHING HERE REFUSES THE PASS. A verdict travels on the item, the
// node below writes it onto the row it belongs to, and the group that
// closes this pass records what happened. A request there was nowhere
// to store is judged all the same: Store Raw Capture's two refusals are
// about the row, this one is about the envelope, and a capture naming a
// source this deployment does not hold is still an envelope that was or
// was not well formed.
//
// The one throw is about the canvas rather than about the capture. One
// request is one item here, the trigger, the context read and the store
// each answering exactly one, so a count other than one means a node
// between them started answering per something else and this item's
// verdict would be written onto a row it is not about.
//
// ONE ITEM IN, ONE ITEM OUT. The posted body is read back off
// $('Capture Webhook').first().json.body rather than copied forward by
// every node between, which is the handle every node on this canvas has
// on the request. What $input carries is the store's answer, and the
// node below reads this node's answer by name for the body it accepted.

// How several faults about one envelope are joined, which is the
// separator ar-ingest's Extract Records joins contract divergences
// with.
const REFUSAL_JOIN = '; ';

// Which envelope member carries the body, and which one states the
// contract version. Spelled here rather than reached for, the same way
// src/sources/push-capture.ts spells its own copy: the names are the
// wire names, and a node defining them in terms of a field-map
// convention would move which member is read the next time that
// convention is renamed.
const BODY_MEMBER = 'body';
const VERSION_MEMBER = 'version';

// What documents.parse_error says once the boundary has accepted an
// envelope and before anything has extracted from it. A constant, and
// it REPLACES Store Raw Capture's own constant rather than being added
// to it: that sentence says nothing has judged the capture, which
// stopped being true the moment this node answered. The row is still
// failed, because nothing has read the body yet, and the group below is
// what promotes it.
const ACCEPTED_NOTE = 'the capture envelope was accepted and nothing '
  + 'has extracted from it since';

// The contract version the client stated, read by own key and read at
// all only so this node can say which refusal fired.
//
// Object.hasOwn rather than a bare read, which is the reading the
// library makes and for the same reason: over an object carrying no
// data at all a bare read answers Object.prototype's own members, so an
// envelope with nothing in it would state a version.
//
// Answers undefined for anything that is not a keyed object, which is
// what lets one comparison cover a payload with no keys as well as one
// stating another number.
function statedVersion(payload) {
  return typeof payload === 'object' && payload !== null
    && !Array.isArray(payload) && Object.hasOwn(payload, VERSION_MEMBER)
    ? payload[VERSION_MEMBER]
    : undefined;
}

const items = $input.all();

if (items.length !== 1) {
  throw new Error(
    '[ar-capture] Judge Capture Envelope expects one item per request: '
    + String(items.length) + ' items reached it',
  );
}

const stored = items[0].json;
const posted = $('Capture Webhook').first().json.body;
const faults = captureEnvelopeErrors(posted);
const accepted = faults.length === 0;
const versionAccepted = statedVersion(posted) === CAPTURE_CONTRACT_VERSION;

// The note, built for an accepted envelope and for no other. Every
// member of it is one the boundary has just read, so each is an own
// key, and none of the four names is one a plain object treats
// specially.
const capture = accepted
  ? Object.fromEntries(
    CAPTURE_ENVELOPE_MEMBERS
      .filter((member) => member !== BODY_MEMBER)
      .map((member) => [member, posted[member]]),
  )
  : null;

return [{
  json: {
    domain_id: stored.domain_id,
    source_id: stored.source_id,
    document_id: stored.document_id,
    document_stored: stored.document_stored,
    store_error: stored.store_error,
    contract_version: CAPTURE_CONTRACT_VERSION,
    contract_version_accepted: versionAccepted,
    envelope_accepted: accepted,
    capture_faults: faults,
    parse_error: accepted
      ? ACCEPTED_NOTE
      : faults.join(REFUSAL_JOIN),
    capture_raw: accepted
      ? { capture, record: posted[BODY_MEMBER] }
      : null,
  },
}];
